    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and both its tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field, derived from an owner's city via the pinned city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/CityRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class holding the fixed table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with `localityOf(city)` returning the canonical region or `UNKNOWN` (including for a null city).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `locality(owner)` default method that delegates to `CityRegion.localityOf(...)`, and a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`. This mirrors the existing derived-field pattern (`initials`, `membershipTier`) rather than growing any method into a catch-all.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nSince `locality` is a pure function of `city`, computing it in the mapper (like the other read-only derived fields) means it's always consistent on `GET`, with the table isolated in its own reusable class. Both acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` for Sydney, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass, and the full suite is green.",
